[4/4] STEP 26/35: LABEL ai.opencharly.description='{"candy":[{"origin":"candy:github.com/opencharly/layer-supervisord","description":"supervisord is the container init that supervises every service and provides a per-user XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\nInstalls the supervisor package, providing /usr/bin/supervisord (PID 1\nfor container images) and the supervisorctl control client. It also\ncreates a per-user /tmp/xdg-runtime directory at mode 0700 and points\nXDG_RUNTIME_DIR at it, so older podman/buildah and wayland/pipewire both\naccept it. Every claim below is observable either in the built image or\nin the running deployment.\n","plan":[{"check":"the supervisord process manager binary is installed","plugin":"file","plugin_input":{"exists":true,"file":"/usr/bin/supervisord"},"intent_do":"assert"},{"check":"the supervisorctl control client is installed","plugin":"file","plugin_input":{"exists":true,"file":"/usr/bin/supervisorctl"},"intent_do":"assert"},{"check":"the supervisor package is recorded in the package database","plugin":"package","plugin_input":{"installed":true,"package":"supervisor"},"intent_do":"assert"},{"check":"a per-user XDG_RUNTIME_DIR directory exists in the image","plugin":"file","plugin_input":{"file":"/tmp/xdg-runtime","filetype":"directory"},"intent_do":"assert"},{"check":"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is exported and points at a /tmp-based per-user runtime dir","plugin":"command","plugin_input":{"command":"[ \"$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\" = /tmp/xdg-runtime ] || [ \"$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\" = /tmp ]\n"},"intent_do":"assert","exit_status":0},{"check":"supervisord runs as container init and its control socket answers supervisorctl pid","plugin":"command","context":["runtime"],"plugin_input":{"command":"supervisorctl pid","in_container":true},"intent_do":"assert","exit_status":0}]},{"origin":"candy:layer-containerd","description":"containerd, installed and configured for the device-less case. It writes a version-2\nconfig.toml on the `native` snapshotter — which needs NO block device, LVM thin pool or\ndevmapper — and hands the running state to a bed that asserts it. Making the snapshotter a\ndeclared value rather than a constant belongs to the typed `containerd:` surface the ledger\nasks for (opencharly/layer-containerd#1), which does not exist yet; the constant here is the\ndevice-less default that surface will keep.\n","plan":[{"check":"the config the daemon will read names the device-less snapshotter","plugin":"command","id":"containerd-config-written","plugin_input":{"command":"grep -q '\''snapshotter = \"native\"'\'' /etc/containerd/config.toml"},"run_as":"root","intent_do":"assert"},{"check":"the daemon the config belongs to is installed","plugin":"command","id":"containerd-installed","plugin_input":{"command":"command -v containerd \u0026\u0026 containerd --version"},"intent_do":"assert"}]}],"box":[{"origin":"box:check-containerd-pod","description":"Disposable bed image for the containerd layer'\''s R10 — a Fedora base composing the layer under test."}]}'
